On Wednesday, August 5, 2015 at 12:28:36 PM UTC-4, Ben Lambert wrote:
> Sorry to ask you again, but have read the article. I can't see within the article the 'mixture of normals' bit that you mention (I see a reference to this on p133, but not elsewhere). I'm sure I'm just being dense, but could you point me to what you mean? How should one create multivariate t distribution-like priors in Stan?

Equation 3, where A is a Cholesky factor of the dispersion matrix for the multivariate t distribution. In other words, iid standard normal priors on the elements of Z and a scaled inverse chi-squared prior on W implies a multivariate student t prior on X with mode mu and dispersion matrix A * A'.

Ben

