On Monday, August 10, 2015 at 10:08:58 PM UTC+2, Jonah wrote:
> Regarding the question about the length of the chains: there's no point in running them that long unless you really need to (e.g. takes that long to converge). If the markov chain isn't geometrically ergodic then by running the chains for a really long time you might suddenly see undesirable behavior, which is a big red flag, but in general if there's convergence then you only need as many draws as will give you a good effective sample size for your goals.

