Bob, if you have a parameter

real y;

and you put a prior

y ~ uniform(-1,1)

I can understand if you say that it won't be super-efficient compared to "real<lower=-1,upper=1> y;"  but is it really true that it won't work? (ie. will it give you wrong answers in the limit of a large number of samples?)

