On Friday, August 21, 2015 at 7:39:35 PM UTC-7, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> How would you go about treating the unmeasured "true" value
> as a latent variable?  Isn't that mu in this repeated measurement
> of the same item situation?

There are two underlying "true" variables, one is the "true" weight, and the other is the "true" pre-rounding error.

since y_obs = true_weight  + true_underlying_normal_measurement_error + true_rounding_error

and this is exact,

you can calculate the true_underlying_normal_measurement_error samples from your data, just

y_obs - y_err - mu

