I agree your model corresponds to the generative model you are trying to create. I want to say that Bob's model is a different model which is valid under some kind of circumstances, but I'm going to have to think more carefully about what those are, and whether that's true. One intuition I have here is that the uniform maxent priors on the  roundoff errors don't appear in your model. Your model should be more efficient because of that.

btw: did you generate those data from some particular normal RNG + roundoff, so that you know the "true" parameters?

one thing to do here I think is to look at the limit of somewhat larger datasets to see if the models converge to the same thing asymptotically, and whether bob's model is biased etc.

