:-)  That rounding_latent.stan is exactly the same as mine other than
that you define an intermediate transformed parameter.

But your rounding_latent_2.stan is exactly what Daniel Lakeland originally
proposed, and I replied suggesting rounding_latent.stan because the
latent_2 version has parameter declarations that don't match their support.

I was just about to send in another post in the original thread showing
how marginalizing out the error variables in rounding_latent.stan gives
you the same density as rounding_integrated.stan.

I think I'd also write it this way

 log(normal_cdf(y[n] + 0.5, mu, sigma)
     - normal_cdf(y[n] - 0.5, mu, sigma))

just to make it clear what's going on (rather than scaling and translating
the unit cdf function Phi()).

- Bob

