Dear Ben, Andrew, STAN users,

the model works perfectly fine now. I attached the to whoever wants to use it.
Feel free, for any purpose.

The ARMA model on:
6.4 pg. 84 2.7.0 shows:
nu[1] <- mu + phi * mu;   // assume err[0] == 0

Isn't with err[0] == 0 the model AR(1) and thus nu[1] should be

nu[1] <- mu / (1-phi);

Here's a link to Expected Value of ARMA(1,1):
http://mathhelpforum.com/advanced-statistics/178529-expected-value-variance-arma-1-1-model.html

 I changed Ben's suggestions slightly:

  for (t in 2:T)  nu[t] <- mu + phi * nu[t-1] + sigma * nu_z[t];

Andre

