Hi,
I don't have time to look at the model in detail.
but one thing that might be an issue i that the 150 trials
you have are not a lot to allow a reliable estimation of parameters, I believe.

Here is some code for a simple parameter recovery test that shows that
one can recover wfpt distribution parameters with acceptable accuracy with stan:
https://github.com/gbiele/stan_wiener_test

maybe you can compare this with your code to see what the problem might be.

One issue I have not been able to solve is that using the wiener in stan
requires lots of RAM. For the simple test in the linked code, 2500 trials
(500 per condition) is already too much for a machine with 8GB RAM.
(using rstan, I haven't tested that in cmdstan yet)

guido

